{
  "nodes": [
    {
      "id": "1000000000000001",
      "type": "group",
      "x": -80,
      "y": -80,
      "width": 1740,
      "height": 1060,
      "label": "Vaultman Test Audit - 2026-05-17",
      "color": "5"
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000002",
      "type": "file",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 360,
      "height": 180,
      "file": ".agents/docs/work/hardening/research/2026-05-17-test-audit/index.md"
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000003",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 440,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "# Suite Snapshot\n\n219 test files / 1283 `it` or `test` calls.\n\n- Unit: 139 files / 880 tests\n- Component: 72 files / 395 tests\n- Integration: 7 files / 13 tests"
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000004",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 940,
      "y": 20,
      "width": 420,
      "height": 180,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# Best-Practice Baseline\n\nTDD should preserve a fast red/green loop. The suite should follow the pyramid: many fast unit tests, fewer integration tests, and scarce end-to-end/live checks."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000005",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "# F1 Stale Mirror-Class Tests\n\n4 component files fail around `.nav-file`, `.tree-item`, and `.metadata-property`.\n\nLikely cause: tests set `mode`/`identity`, while current `useNativeDom` derives from `activePreset.useNativeDom`."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000006",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 510,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "1",
      "text": "# F2 Legacy ThemePreset Test\n\n`test/unit/mainThemeSettingsSync.test.ts` uses a legacy preset shape.\n\nCurrent presets require `source`, `displayName`, `useNativeDom`, tokenized `density`, and current dock/tabs/view mode fields."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000007",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": 280,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "2",
      "text": "# F3 Slow Component Gate\n\n`pnpm test:component` took about 585s and failed 8 tests.\n\nKeep it as a wide gate, but do not use it as the default TDD loop."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000008",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 590,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "# F4 Harness Diagnostics\n\nLikely product-gate cleanup candidates:\n\n- `manual-register.test.ts`\n- `debug-path.test.ts`\n\nThey validate infrastructure or environment state more than Vaultman behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000009",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 510,
      "y": 590,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "3",
      "text": "# F5 Uneven Coverage\n\nGlobal unit coverage passes, but some risk areas remain low/uncovered:\n\n- `serviceCMenu.ts`\n- `serviceSnippetsIndex.ts`\n- `serviceSuggestModal.ts`\n- `inputModal.ts`\n- `serviceNodeFieldVisibility.ts`"
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000010",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1000,
      "y": 590,
      "width": 430,
      "height": 230,
      "color": "4",
      "text": "# Recommended Next Actions\n\n1. Fix mirror-class setup with `setPreset('native')`.\n2. Fix or remove legacy ThemePreset test.\n3. Move harness diagnostics out of product gate.\n4. Add focused component gates.\n5. Test uncovered risk modules by behavior."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000011",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 640,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "5",
      "text": "# Triage Rule\n\nKeep a test when it protects public behavior or a documented compatibility contract. Update it when the behavior is still valid but setup references an old contract. Archive it when it only proves the harness works."
    },
    {
      "id": "1000000000000012",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 750,
      "y": 880,
      "width": 680,
      "height": 160,
      "color": "6",
      "text": "# Functional Coverage Targets\n\nData safety, Explorer runtime, theme compatibility, Obsidian command/context-menu integration, keyboard/accessibility behavior, and live `plugin-dev` smoke harnesses."
    }
  ],
